#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gametype:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arcade, Sport"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of possible players:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Ten</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; is a miniature golf game with 2d top-down view. Courses are "
"dynamic, and up to 10 people can play at once in competition."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; comes with a tutorial course. <link linkend=\"howto\">Playing "
"this course</link> is the easiest way to get started."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Objective:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Put the ball into the hole with the least possible hits."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname;'s game-play is simple. It is the easiest to learn how to play "
"hands-on, and thus a tutorial course is included to guide you through the "
"basics. This chapter will guide you through this tutorial. To start the "
"tutorial, choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Help</guimenu><guimenuitem>Tutorial</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hitting the Ball"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To aim the ball, either line up the mouse behind the ball so the putter aims "
"in the direction you want to hit it or press one of the <keycap>Left Arrow</"
"keycap> (counterclockwise) or <keycap>Right Arrow</keycap> (clockwise) keys, "
"to rotate the putter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To rotate the putter more quickly with the keyboard, hold down "
"<keycap>Shift</keycap> while pressing or holding the arrow keys. To rotate "
"more slowly, hold down <keycap>Control</keycap>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To hit the ball, press and hold either the &LMB; or <keycap>Down Arrow</"
"keycap> key. The longer you hold down the key or button, the more strength "
"the putt will have. It will take practice to get a good feel for speed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To stop abort the putt while you are still holding moving the putter back in "
"your stroke, press <keycap>Escape</keycap>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hit the ball into the hole to move on to the next."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:95 index.docbook:780
#, no-c-format
msgid "Slopes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Slopes are slanted areas of the course that the golf ball rolls down in an "
"expected manner. The light of the golf course is from the upper-left, so the "
"brightest slopes will push the ball towards the upper-left corner of the "
"hole. Choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Hole</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Info</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> to see an arrow that points in the direction the "
"slope will roll the ball."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tutorial hole, hit the ball onto the upward-pointing slope and let "
"it roll into the cup to move onto the next hole."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the next hole, experiment with the other kinds of slopes. There are "
"elliptical, vertical, horizontal, and diagonal slopes in &kappname;. Hit the "
"ball into the hole."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "Steepness"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next tutorial hole has two slopes of differing steepness. If you choose "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Hole</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Info</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>, the steepness of the slope will appear as a number from 1-8, "
"where 8 is steepest and 1 is shallowest. Hit the ball into the hole and "
"continue to the next hole."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Walls"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Balls bounce of walls as one would expect them to, with a little bit of "
"dampening. Deflect the ball off the walls and into the cup to advance to the "
"next hole."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:112 index.docbook:809
#, no-c-format
msgid "Puddles and Sand"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "Puddles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Puddles are blue. When your ball rolls into a puddle, a penalty stroke is "
"added to your score and you must then choose where you want to take your "
"next shot from: either next to the puddle or from the same place as where "
"you just took the last shot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sand"
msgstr "Sable"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sand is yellow. Balls roll through sand very slowly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hit the ball around the puddles and through the sand into the hole to "
"continue to the next tutorial hole."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:122 index.docbook:830
#, no-c-format
msgid "Windmills"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Windmills are compound objects with brown border walls and a moving arm on "
"one side. Half-walls create the opening to the windmill, which the black arm "
"swings across. It takes practice to be able to time the stroke of the ball "
"to pass through the opening. Hit the ball through the windmill into the hole "
"to continue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Black Holes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you hit your ball into a black hole, it is transported to the exit and "
"ejected at the angle of the exit at a speed directly relational to the speed "
"your ball was going. Choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Hole</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Info</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to see which Black "
"Hole goes to which exit and which direction the ball will come out of the "
"exit. The rim around Black Holes are the same color as their corresponding "
"exits. Hit the ball into the black hole, which will then eject the ball into "
"the cup so you can go to the next hole."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:130 index.docbook:845
#, no-c-format
msgid "Floaters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Floaters are moving platforms that carry a ball that lands on it. Floaters' "
"speeds vary. This one is a pretty slow floater, but you still must time your "
"shot so you can go over the wall and into the cup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bridges"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Bridges are simple - they just lift the ball above the things below them, "
"like slopes, sand, and puddles. They can have brown walls on their perimeter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Rules, Strategies and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's in-depth description of &kappname;'s basic features."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting a Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To start a game, choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Game</guimenu><guimenuitem>New</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. This opens a dialog where you can configure your "
"new game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More third-party &kappname; courses are available at the &kappname; website. "
"See <ulink url=\"http://web.mit.edu/jasonkb/www/kolf/\">the &kappname; user-"
"uploaded courses page</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Players</guilabel> Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a player to your game, click the <guibutton>New Player</guibutton> "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The text boxes in the grass area are the names of the players in this game. "
"To change the name of the players, change the text in the text boxes. To "
"change the ball color of the players' balls, click the middle button that "
"has a color rectangle, and a dialog will open where you can select the new "
"ball color. The rectangle on the button is the current player's ball color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove a player, click the <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> button next to "
"the player's name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Course</guilabel> Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To choose the course that you want to play, click its entry in the list box "
"on the left of this page. &kappname; comes with many built-in courses that "
"you can play."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a course that you have downloaded or made, click on the "
"<guibutton>Add...</guibutton> button on the bottom of this page, and choose "
"the course file in the file dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Options</guilabel> Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this page you can choose whether or not this game will be played in "
"<guilabel>Strict mode</guilabel>. In strict mode, there is no undo, moving "
"holes, or editing of the course. This mode is generally for competition. "
"Only in strict mode are high scores kept."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saved Games"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; can keep a history of your rounds that are still in progress and "
"save them to disk so you can load them and play them later. Saved games "
"include the current hole, names and colors of all players in game, and the "
"scores of the players."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saving Your Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To save your game while still playing, choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Game</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Save Game</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. If you have not "
"saved a game on this game before, you will be prompted for the file to save "
"to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "Loading Your Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To load the game that you saved, choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Game</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Load...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. You can then "
"choose the saved game to open."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "Practicing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a few features that make practicing your golf easier. These "
"features are not enabled during strict mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undo"
msgstr "Anullar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To undo a bad shot, choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Hole</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Undo Shot</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Switching Holes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>Go</guimenu> menu contains many menu items for switching to "
"different holes that are quite self explanatory. See the <link linkend=\"go-"
"menu\"><guimenu>Go</guimenu> menu reference</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "Putting Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; has a few ways to putt. The basic putting method is <link linkend="
"\"hitting\">described above</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mouse is enabled by default. This means that whenever the mouse is "
"moved, the putter aligns to the line between the mouse and ball."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you prefer to only use the keyboard and arrow keys, you can disable mouse "
"putting by unchecking <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Enable Mouse for Moving Putter</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Putting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Advanced putting can be enabled by checking <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Enable Advanced Putting</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. "
"This putting mode is slightly more challenging than the regular click-and-"
"hold mode, and can be used with either the mouse or keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "To putt in this mode:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click or press the <keycap>Down Arrow</keycap> key once to begin the swing. "
"The putting indicator will appear, and the strength gauge will start filling "
"up with a color, which changes as the gauge fills up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click or press the <keycap>Down Arrow</keycap> key when the strength gauge "
"has filled up the amount that you want. The farther around the circle the "
"strength gauge has filled up, the stronger the putt will be. It takes "
"practice to be able to get the correct strength on putts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After this, the color in the putting indicator will start to wind down back "
"to where it started."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click or press the <keycap>Down Arrow</keycap> key again when the strength-"
"indicator is as close as possible to the center line of the putting "
"indicator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The closer the final click (or key press) is, the more true the putt is to "
"the original line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface Overview"
msgstr ""

